td>1.27</td> </tr><tr><td>Walmart</td><td>1.21</td> </tr><tr><td>Visa</td><td>0.72</td> </tr><tr><td>Microsoft</td><td>0.69</td> </tr><tr><td>Eli Lilly and Company</td><td>0.57</td> </tr><tr><td>MasterCard</td><td>0.55</td> </tr><tr><td>Apple</td><td>0.49</td> </tr><tr><td>Meta Platforms</td><td>0.1</td> </tr><tr><td>NVIDIA</td><td>0.01</td> </tr> </tbody> </table></div><p>LONDON STOCK EXCHANGE (LNSTY) ADR Dashboard End-of-Day Fri, Jun 07</p><p>http://www.londonstockexchange.com</p><div class=\"story-table-container\"><table class=\"story-basic-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Last</td><td>$30.36</td><td>Market Cap</td><td>$64 billion</td> </tr><tr><td>P/E</td><td>17.1</td><td>Dividend Yield % (TTM)</td><td>1.2</td> </tr><tr><td>EPS (FY2023)</td><td>$1.39</td><td>DPS (past 12 months)</td><td>$0.4 or 36c</td> </tr><tr><td>Shares Outstanding</td><td>2,120,000,000</td><td>Exchange</td><td>INTERNATIONAL DEPOSITORY RECEIPTS [USOTC]</td> </tr><tr><td>Institutional Ownership</td><td>309,374</td><td>% of shares outstanding</td><td>0.01%</td> </tr><tr><td>EPS Growth (FY2023 vs FY2022)</td><td>-40.6%</td><td>Sector</td><td>Diversified Financial Services [of 118 stocks]</td> </tr><tr><td>Today's Volume</td><td>68,000</td><td>Today's VI*</td><td>0.4</td> </tr><tr><td>Ave Daily Volume</td><td>191,544 ADRs</td><td>PV$1000 (1 yr)</td><td>$1,132</td> </tr><tr><td>52-Week Price Range</td><td>24.44 - 30.78</td><td></td><td> </td></tr> </tbody> </table></div><p>VI* Volume Index = Number of shares traded today/Average number of shares traded per day.</p><p>A year ago the London Stock Exchange adr price was $27.17. $1,000 would have bought 36.8 London Stock Exchange adr on that day. Those 36.8 ADRs would be worth $1,117 at today's adr price of $30.36. Dividends reinvested are worth $15. PV$1000= $1,132.</p><p>*Total ADRs Held by Institutions 309,374; equivalent to 77,344 London Stock Exchange shares on issue. This represents 0.01% of total shares on issue.</p><p>Activities</p><p>London Stock Exchange Group plc is the United Kingdom's primary stock exchange. The LSE provides markets that facilitate the raising of capital and the trading of corporate securities, access to a trading environment, as well as real-time pricing and reference information services worldwide. Market coverage includes equities, derivatives and fixed-interest securities. It is the International Depository Receipt (IDR) market's 2nd largest Diversified financial services company by market capitalisation.</p><p>Top Management and Board of Directors</p><p>Top Management</p><p>Top Management [One top executive with tenure &gt; 5 yrs]</p><div class=\"story-table-container\"><table class=\"story-basic-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Name</td><td>Designation</td><td>Since Appointment</td> </tr><tr><td>David Schwimmer</td><td>Chief Executive Officer, Executive Director, Interim Group Head - Data &amp; Analytics</td><td>5 Yrs, 10 Mos</td> </tr> </tbody> </table></div><p>Top Management [Six top executives with tenure &lt; 4 yrs]</p><div class=\"story-table-container\"><table class=\"story-basic-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Name</td><td>Designation</td><td>Since Appointment</td> </tr><tr><td>Anna Manz</td><td>Chief Financial Officer, Executive Director</td><td>3 Yrs, 11 Mos</td> </tr><tr><td>Donald Robert</td><td>Non-Executive Chairman</td><td>-</td> </tr><tr><td>David Shalders</td><td>Chief Operating Officer</td><td>-</td> </tr><tr><td>Lisa M. Condron</td><td>Company Secretary</td><td>-</td> </tr><tr><td>Daniel Maguire</td><td>Chief Strategy Officer, Group Head - Post Trade</td><td>-</td> </tr><tr><td>Balbir Bakhshi</td><td>Chief Risk Officer</td><td>-</td> </tr> </tbody> </table></div><p>Board Of Directors</p><p>Board Of Directors [Seven directors with tenure &lt; 5 yrs]</p><div class=\"story-table-container\"><table class=\"story-basic-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Name</td><td>Designation</td><td>Since Appointment</td> </tr><tr><td>Martin J. Brand</td><td>Non-Executive Director</td><td>3 Yrs, 5 Mos</td> </tr><tr><td>Dominic Blakemore</td><td>Non-Executive Independent Director</td><td>4 Yrs, 5 Mos</td> </tr><tr><td>Tsega Gebreyes</td><td>Non-Executive Independent Director</td><td>3 Yrs, 5 Mos</td> </tr><tr><td>Val Rahmani</td><td>Independent Non-Executive Director</td><td>-</td> </tr><tr><td>William Vereker</td><td>Non-Executive Director</td><td>-</td> </tr><tr><td>Scott Guthrie</td><td>Non-Executive Director</td><td>-</td> </tr><tr><td>Kathleen Traynor Derose</td><td>Non-Executive Independent Director</td><td>-</td> </tr> </tbody> </table></div><p>Profiles of Board of Directors</p><p>Val Rahmani</p><p>Independent Non-Executive Director</p><p>Appointed to the Board in December 2017</p><p>Key areas of experience: Technology, technical risk management, corporate governance, strategy, sales and marketing.</p><p>Val brings significant expertise and knowledge of technology and technical risk management to the Board gained from almost 30 years with IBM and 4 years as CEO of a cyber security start up.</p><p>Val has wide-ranging experience as a senior executive in the technology sector fulfilling the role of general manager, board member, start up mentor, management consultant and public speaker. Val also holds a DPhil in Chemistry from the University of Oxford.</p><p>Relevant past experience: Val is a former Non-Executive Director of Aberdeen Asset Management plc and Teradici Corporation.</p><p>Other current appointments: Val currently serves as a Non-Executive Director and member of the Audit Committee at RenaissanceRe Holdings Limited. She is also a Non-Executive Director of Computer Task Group Inc, where she chairs the Compensation Committee and serves as a member of the Audit and Governance Committees and a Non-Executive Director of the early stage company, Rungway.</p><p>Created by <a href=\"http://www.buysellsignals.com\" data-type=\"url\" class=\"tr-link\" translate=\"no\">www.buysellsignals.com</a> </p></div></div>"
